# Keep the Docker build context small and free of secrets/junk.
# Anything matched here is NOT sent to the daemon or copied by `COPY . .`.
#
# ALLOWLIST (2026-10-22): ignore everything, then re-include only what the two
# images run. The old denylist let a local `COPY . .` sweep in infra/ (terraform
# state + tfvars, a 1.5 GB nba_data.sql dump, 1.5 GB of provider binaries),
# web/ (node_modules, .next, .env.local) and .venv-bedrock/ — a 9.44 GB image
# that should be ~3 GB. New top-level folders are now excluded by default; add a
# `!folder/` line here if an image ever needs one.
*

# Code packages (Dockerfile.api copies only api/; Dockerfile.pipeline copies all)
!api/
!core/
!data_engineering/
!modeling/
!orchestration/
!scripts/

# Requirements (Dockerfile.pipeline copies these explicitly before the code)
!requirements.txt
!requirements-pipeline.txt

# Re-exclude junk INSIDE the allowed folders (later rules win)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/*.md
**/.env
**/.env.*
